  "engine.guide.claude.title": "Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)",
  "@engine.guide.claude.title": {
    "description": "Title (after ✨) of a setup guide in Help."
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.who": "Everyone",
  "@engine.guide.claude.who": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): who the guide is for (after 👤)."
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.step1": "Account menu → 📚 Subjects → **✨ Create a subject with Claude** (or the same button in the subject picker). The window shows every step, numbered, with ⓘ tips.",
  "@engine.guide.claude.step1": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 1. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.step2": "**Way A — here in noema-lite:** create a Claude Console account (platform.claude.com), add a little credit, create an API key and paste it in the window. noema-lite uploads the skill, sends your files to Claude and imports the finished subject — you never leave the app. You see the cost live and set a limit.",
  "@engine.guide.claude.step2": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 2. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.step3": "**Way B — in the Claude app or website:** with your Claude plan (Free, Pro, Max): switch on code execution, add the connector **Customize → Connectors → + Add → Add custom connector** with the address {mcp} (the same for everyone and every device), then attach your sources in a new chat and send the prompt from the window.",
  "@engine.guide.claude.step3": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 3. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them. mcp = the connector’s address.",
    "placeholders": {
      "mcp": {
        "type": "String",
        "example": "https://noema.example.org/mcp"
      }
    }
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.step4": "**Way C — a whole Roadmap with your Claude plan (⭐ recommended for Roadmaps, usually the cheapest):** set up the connector as in way B, then in 🧭 Roadmaps choose **💬 Claude app** when you create or import a Roadmap. Copy the one message noema-lite shows into a Claude chat: Claude builds the Roadmap, plans the chapters and prepares the queued steps; they appear on the Roadmap by themselves. No API cost — the bigger the Roadmap, the bigger the saving.",
  "@engine.guide.claude.step4": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 4. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.step5": "Claude reads everything, adds pictures (from your sources, from the web and its own diagrams / graphs) and builds the pack; the new subject appears in your picker.",
  "@engine.guide.claude.step5": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 5. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.step6": "Share it if you like: 🔗 on the subject → public (🌍 Explore) or with one person.",
  "@engine.guide.claude.step6": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 6. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.note1": "Way A: your API key stays on this device only. Way B: noema-lite never sees your Claude login.",
  "@engine.guide.claude.note1": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): note 1 (after 💡). Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.claude.note2": "Updates are additive: Claude keeps all ids, so your progress stays.",
  "@engine.guide.claude.note2": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Set up Claude and create subjects (three ways)” (Account menu › ❓ Help): note 2 (after 💡). Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.title": "Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.title": {
    "description": "Title (after 🧭) of a setup guide in Help."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.who": "Everyone with a Claude API key or a Gemini key",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.who": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): who the guide is for (after 👤)."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.step1": "Subject picker → **🧭 Roadmaps** (or 🧭 in the top bar) → **➕ New Roadmap**.",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.step1": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 1. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.step2": "Type what you want to master, your starting point and the depth. Four AI agents lay it out: **every prerequisite** (from several sciences), **the whole goal** (aspects, sub-topics, synthesis) and **applications**; then they plan the chapters of every step.",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.step2": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 2. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.step3": "The Roadmap shows three parts. **open** steps (green open padlock) can be studied; **🔒 locked** ones show their information and chapters but open only when their prerequisites are mastered.",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.step3": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 3. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.step4": "Every step becomes a full subject (theory, exercises, flashcards, drills, tutor), prepared in the background a few steps ahead while the app is open — with Claude from official sources found on the web, or with Gemini and Google Search.",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.step4": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 4. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.step5": "A step is **✅ mastered** when all its sections are read and 80 % of its exercises solved — or with **🎓 I already know this** (8 of 10 in a short test).",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.step5": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 5. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.step6": "Already have a subject for a step? On the step: **📦 Use a subject I have**. Only that step is re-planned to follow the subject (🔄 until its new plan is here); it is never generated. Subjects on no step wait on the **📚 Shelf** (bottom of the subject picker): study them there, or **🧭 Put on a Roadmap…**.",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.step6": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): step 6. Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.note1": "Roadmaps and prepared steps are saved in your account (cloud) like your subjects.",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.note1": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): note 1 (after 💡). Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
  "engine.guide.curricula.note2": "Claude costs a few dollars per prepared step (limit per step in ⚙️ of the Roadmap); Gemini’s free quota is limited.",
  "@engine.guide.curricula.note2": {
    "description": "Setup guide “Roadmaps: from a goal to a Roadmap of steps” (Account menu › ❓ Help): note 2 (after 💡). Markdown: keep **bold**, `code`, links and file names; use the same names for the app’s buttons and menus as your translation of them."
  },
